  <name>Software</name>
  <summary>Install and update apps</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      An unofficial and experimental fork of GNOME Software, the app store of
      the GNOME desktop. It is not made or supported by the GNOME Software
      developers or the GNOME project; please report problems to the fork.
      The fork's changes were developed with the help of generative AI.
    </p>
    <p>
      Like GNOME Software, it lets you find and install Flatpak apps, the
      packages of your distribution (through PackageKit, dnf5 or rpm-ostree)
      and snaps, keeps them and your firmware up to date, and manages your
      software repositories. The fork has a new core: every page shows the
      same state and progress of an app, and lists update in place instead
      of being reloaded.
    </p>
    <p>
      It replaces the Software of your system: the desktop opens it for app
      details and search, and it checks for updates in the background once
      you turn that on. Your settings are shared with the system's Software.
    </p>
  </description>
